ck of a test suite makes it impossible to fully verify that the layering adheres to the “clean architecture” style required by the internal docs.\n\n### PR\u202f#1 considerations\nThe compliance scan was performed on the working tree. To fully assess the impact of **pull request #1**, the diff introduced by that PR should be reviewed (e.g., via `git diff origin/main...origin/pr/1`). Typical red flags to look for in the PR are:\n- Adding source files outside the `src/` tree.\n- Introducing new top\u2011level directories that are not part of the approved set.\n- Renaming or moving existing modules in a way that breaks the prescribed package boundaries.\n\nUntil the PR diff is examined, the static scan above represents the baseline state.\n\n### Recommendations\n1. **Add a top\u2011level `tests/` directory** with unit\u2011test scaffolding (`__init__.py`, a sample test file) to resolve the hard violation.\n2. **Create a `CHANGELOG.md`** at the repository root to satisfy the soft recommendation.\n3. Review PR\u202f#1’s file changes for any new top\u2011level paths or violations of the module naming conventions before merging.\n\n---\n\n```json\n{\n  "Name": "ArchitectureConcierge",\n  "Inquiry": "Compare the structure of the repository gokul04/onlinebookstore (and the changes in pull request https://github.com/gokul04/onlinebookstore/pull/1) against internal engineering documentation guidelines. Identify any hard violations of required structure, layering, naming, or modularity conventions, as well as soft/advisory issues.",\n  "Mode": "Fulfill",\n  "Response": "The compliance scan found a high\u2011severity hard violation: the required top\u2011level `tests/` directory is missing. A low\u2011severity soft recommendation is to add a `CHANGELOG.md`. The repository is currently non\u2011compliant. No additional layering or modularity violations were reported by the static check. A detailed assessment of PR\u202f#1 should include reviewing the diff for any new top\u2011level paths or naming issues."\n}\n```'}
