2026-10-22 13:40:44 Mitteleuropäische Sommerzeit | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow: {"type": "AI", "text": "# Go/No-Go Readiness Report**PR:** https://github.com/gokul04/onlinebookstore/pull/1\n**Repository:** `C:\\progs\\hackathon\\code_repo\\onlinebookstore`\n**Date:** Release readiness assessment\n\n---\n\n## Overall Verdict: **NO-GO**\n\nTwo independent blocking conditions are present: a **high-severity security finding** and **hard architecture violations**. Test coverage could not be verified at all, which is a third unresolved risk.\n\n---\n\n## Security Findings\n\n| Severity | Finding | Location | OWASP |\n|----------|---------|----------|-------|\n| **HIGH** | Hardcoded password | `src/main/java/com/bittercode/constant/db/UsersDBConstants.java:8` | A02:2021 Cryptographic Failures, A07:2021 Identification & Authentication Failures |\n\n**Dependency scan:** `pom.xml` (Maven) — **no vulnerable or outdated packages detected** (A06:2021 clean).\n\n**Severity distribution:** Critical: 0 · High: 1 · Medium: 0 · Low: 0\n\n---\n\n## Architecture Findings\n\n**Compliance status: ❌ Non-compliant**\n\n**Hard violations (blocking):**\n- Missing required directory `tests/` at repository root\n- Missing required file `README.md` in `src/` and `WebContent/`\n- Missing required directory `src/` within `src/` and `WebContent/` *(likely a tool artifact — flag for confirmation)*\n- Missing required directory `tests/` within `src/` and `WebContent/`\n\n**Soft recommendations (non-blocking):**\n- Missing `CHANGELOG.md` at root, in `src/`, and in `WebContent/`\n- Missing recommended `docs/` directory at root, in `src/`, and in `WebContent/`\n- Missing `.gitignore` in `src/` and `WebContent/`\n\nLayering, naming, and modularity conventions were **not assessed** by the automated check — only file/directory presence was verified. The top level mixes configuration files, scripts, and web resources, which may conflict with separation-of-concerns guidelines but needs manual review.\n\n---\n\n## QA / Test Coverage Findings\n\n| Metric | Result |\n|--------|--------|\n| Coverage percentage | **Unavailable** — no coverage report found (`coverage.xml`, JUnit XML, or text summary all absent) |\n| Tests passed / failed / skipped | **Unavailable** — no test execution logs found |\n| Meets 80% threshold | **Unverifiable** |\n\nNo test or coverage artifacts exist in the repository. Combined with the architecture finding that no `tests/` directory exists, this strongly suggests **there is no automated test suite at all** — in which case coverage is effectively 0%, far below the 80% threshold.\n\n---\n\n## Blocking Issues (must fix before release)\n\n1. **Hardcoded password in `UsersDBConstants.java:8`** — externalize to an environment variable or secrets manager; rotate the credential if it was ever committed to a shared repository or deployed.\n2. **Missing top-level `tests/` directory** — required by engineering standards. Add the test suite (test sources plus a `README.md`/`src`/`tests` structure per the compliance rules for `src/` and `WebContent/`).\n3. **Coverage cannot be demonstrated** — generate and publish a coverage report (e.g. JaCoCo via Maven) alongside the test run, then confirm coverage clears the 80% threshold. Treat as failing until evidence exists.\n4. **Missing `README.md` in `src/` and `WebContent/`** — required files per the structure guidelines.\n\n---\n\n## Non-Blocking Recommendations\n\n- Add `CHANGELOG.md` and a `docs/` directory at the repository root, `src/`, and `WebContent/`.\n- Add `.gitignore` entries under `src/` and `WebContent/`.\n- Add a SAST step to CI — the current scanners cover secrets and dependency CVEs but not injection, insecure deserialization, or authz flaws.\n- Re-run the dependency scanner on every `pom.xml` change to catch new CVEs.\n- Manually review the PR diff for new secrets or injection vectors (see caveat below).\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ Important Caveat on PR Scope\n\nNone of the three review tools could