2026-10-22 14:41:02 Mitteleuropäische Sommerzeit | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-22 14:41:02 - release_readiness - INFO - {'otrace': ['release_manager'], 'text': 'result from security_auditor\n## Security Audit — Release Readiness\n\n**Target:** `gokul04/onlinebookstore` PR #1 · **Local checkout:** `C:\\progs\\hackathon\\code_repo\\onlinebookstore`\n\n---\n\n### Executive Summary\n\nBoth automated scans executed cleanly against the local checkout. **Zero findings were returned by either tool**, so there are **no critical or high severity issues to report** and, on the evidence available, **nothing from these two scans blocks the release**. This is a clean result — but it is a *narrow* clean result, and the scope you requested extends well beyond what pattern-matching scanners can cover. The gap analysis in the OWASP section below is the important part of this report.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Secret / Hardcoded Credential Scan\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Tool | `SecretScannerTool` |\n| Files scanned | **82** |\n| Findings | **0** |\n\nNo API keys, passwords, tokens, or private keys were matched in the source tree. No file paths or line numbers to report.\n\n**Mapping:** the scanner tags this check against **A02:2021 Cryptographic Failures** and **A07:2021 Identification and Authentication Failures** — these are the categories a secret finding *would* have been filed under. With zero findings, neither category is implicated.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Dependency / Known-CVE Scan\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Tool | `VulnerabilityScannerTool` |\n| **Manifests reviewed** | **`pom.xml`** (Maven — the only manifest present) |\n| Findings | **0** |\n\nNo dependencies in `pom.xml` matched a known-vulnerable version signature. **A06:2021 Vulnerable and Outdated Components is not implicated** by this scan.\n\n> **Manifest coverage note:** only `pom.xml` was found. There is no `package.json`, `requirements.txt`, `pom.xml` variant, Gradle build file, Docker base image reference, or lockfile in scope. If this project ships any frontend assets, container images, or vendored jars, those are **unreviewed**.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Severity-Ranked Findings\n\n| Severity | Count | Details |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Critical** | 0 | — |\n| **High** | 0 | — |\n| **Medium** | 0 | — |\n| **Low** | 0 | — |\n| **Informational** | 2 | (a) Scanner coverage limited to `pom.xml`; (b) Manual-review OWASP categories unverified — see §4 |\n\nNo file paths or line numbers are listed because the tools returned no findings. I want to be explicit rather than pad the report: an empty findings table here reflects **tool coverage limits, not a verified absence of flaws**.\n\n---\n\n### 4. OWASP Top 10 — Coverage Analysis\n\nYour scope named six specific concerns. Here is honestly what was and was not evaluated:\n\n| OWASP Category | In your scope? | Evaluated? | Basis |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **A02** Cryptographic Failures | \u2705 | \u26a0\ufe0f Partially | Secret-pattern scan only. Did **not** evaluate TLS config, cipher suites, hashing algorithms for stored credentials, or encryption-at-rest. |\n| **A07** Identification & Authentication Failures | \u2705 | \u26a0\ufe0f Partially | Secret-pattern scan only. Did **not** evaluate session management, password hashing, MFA, credential-stuffing defenses, or auth flow logic. |\n| **A06** Vulnerable & Outdated Components | \u2705 | \u2705 Yes | `pom.xml` scanned; 0 vulnerable versions. |\n| **A03** Injection (SQL/NoSQL/LDAP/Command) | \u2705 | \u274c **No** | Not in scanner capability. Requires manual query-construction review. |\n| **A01** Broken Access Control / Authorization | \u2705 | \u274c **No** | Not in scanner capability. Requires manual RBAC/IDOR review. |\n| **A04** Insecure Design | \u2705 | \u274c **No** | Not in scanner capability. |\n| **A05** Security Misconfiguration | \u2705 | \u274c **No** | Not in scanner capability. Requires manual review of framework defaults, debug flags, CORS, headers, error pages. |\n| **A08** Software & Data Integrity Failures | \u2795 | \u274c **No** | Not in scanner capability. Relevant given CI/CD and dependency pinning. |\n| **A09** Logging & Monitoring Failures | \u2795 | \u274c **No** | Not in scanner capability. Audit-log presence for auth/security events. |\n| **A10** SSRF | \u2795 | \u274c **No** | Not in scanner capability. |\n\n**Categories that could not be evaluated: A03 (Injection), A01 (Broken Access Control), A04 (Insecure Design), A05 (Security Misconfiguration), A08 (Data Integrity Failures), A09 (Logging & Monitoring Failures), A10 (SSRF).**\n\nAlso unevaluated within A02/A07: cryptographic implementation quality, session/cookie flags, password storage hashing.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Release Gate Verdict\n\n**Recommendation: Conditionally release-ready.**\n\n- **No critical or high finding from the executed scans.** Nothing identified blocks release.\n- **This is not a full OWASP compliance attestation.** Six of the ten categories, and five of the six concerns you explicitly named, remain **unverified**.\n- **Before merge, manually confirm** — at minimum: (1) all DB access is parameterized/prepared statements [A03]; (2) every state-changing endpoint enforces authorization, not just authentication [A01]; (3) production has debug mode off, secure error pages without stack traces, and restrictive CORS [A05]; (4) passwords are bcrypt/scrypt/argon2 with per-user salt [A02/A07]; (5) cookies set `HttpOnly` + `Secure` + `SameSite` [A07].\n\n### Additional Caveats on Scope Fidelity\n\n- I audited the **local filesystem checkout** only. I could not verify that the working tree at `C:\\progs\\hackathon\\code_repo\\onlinebookstore` corresponds to PR #1\'s head commit — a `git fetch` + diff against `pull/1/head` is advisable so the audit reflects the actual merge candidate.\n- Secret scanners are **pattern-based** and reliably miss secrets in non-standard formats (encrypted blobs, base64-encoded values, split across variables, credentials in external config consumed at runtime). A 0-finding result lowers but does not eliminate the risk.\n- The CVE check matches **known-vulnerable versions**. It does not detect abandoned/unmaintained packages, typosquatting, or newly disclosed CVEs post-scan.\n\n---\n\n```json\n{\n  "Name": "Security Auditor",\n  "Inquiry": "Security audit for release readiness of pull request https://github.com/gokul04/onlinebookstore/pull/1 in repository gokul04/onlinebookstore, local checkout at C:\\\\progs\\\\hackathon\\\\code_repo\\\\onlinebookstore. Scope: scan for hardcoded secrets, vulnerable/known-CVE dependencies, OWASP compliance issues (injection, auth/authz flaws, insecure deserialization, improper error handling, missing input validation, security misconfiguration). Please report findings severity-ranked (critical/high/medium/low) with file paths and line numbers, and note whether any critical/high issue blocks release. Also report the dependency manifest(s) reviewed and any OWASP categories that could not be evaluated.",\n  "Mode": "Fulfill",\n  "Response": "SECURITY AUDIT - RELEASE READINESS | Target: gokul04/onlinebookstore PR #1 | Checkout: C:\\\\progs\\\\hackathon\\\\code_repo\\\\onlinebookstore\\n\\nEXECUTIVE SUMMARY: Both automated scans ran clean against the local checkout. SecretScannerTool scanned 82 files and returned 0 findings. VulnerabilityScannerTool reviewed the single manifest found (pom.xml) and returned 0 findings. Therefore no critical or high severity issues were identified, and nothing from these scans blocks release. This is a narrow clean result - the scanner capability does not cover most of the requested OWASP scope, which is detailed below.\\n\\n1) SECRET SCAN (SecretScannerTool): 82 files scanned, 0 findings. No hardcoded API keys, passwords, tokens, or private keys matched. No file paths/line numbers to report. Tagged categories A02:2021 Cryptographic Failures and A07:2021 Identification and Authentication Failures are NOT implicated, since no findings were produced in either.\\n\\n2) DEPENDENCY SCAN (VulnerabilityScannerTool): Manifests reviewed: pom.xml (Maven - the only manifest present). 0 known-vulnerable versions found. A06:2021 Vulnerable and Outdated Components is NOT implicated. Coverage note: no package.json, requirements.txt, Gradle file, lockfile, or container base image was in scope, so any frontend assets, images, or vendored jars are unreviewed.\\n\\n3) SEVERITY-RANKED FINDINGS: Critical 0, High 0, Medium 0, Low 0, Informational 2 - (a) dependency scanner coverage limited to pom.xml only; (b) manual-review OWASP categories remain unverified. No file paths or line numbers are listed because no findings were returned; the empty table reflects tool coverage limits rather than verified absence of flaws.\\n\\n4) OWASP TOP 10 COVERAGE: A06 Vulnerable and Outdated Components - EVALUATED (pom.xml, 0 vulns). A02 Cryptographic Failures - PARTIAL (secret-pattern scan only; TLS config, cipher suites, password hashing, encryption-at-rest not evaluated). A07 Identification and Authentication Failures - PARTIAL (secret scan only; session management, password hashing, auth flow logic not evaluated). NOT EVALUATED: A03 Injection (SQL/NoSQL/LDAP/command), A01 Broken Access Control/Authorization, A04 Insecure Design, A05 Security Misconfiguration, A08 Software and Data Integrity Failures, A09 Logging and Monitoring Failures, A10 SSRF. Within A02/A07, cryptographic implementation quality and cookie flags (HttpOnly/Secure/SameSite) are also unevaluated.\\n\\n5) RELEASE GATE: Conditionally release-ready. No critical/high issue identified blocks release, but this is NOT a full OWASP compliance attestation - six of ten categories and five of six explicitly requested concerns remain unverified. Pre-merge manual confirmation recommended for: (1) all DB access parameterized/prepared statements [A03]; (2) authorization enforced on every state-changing endpoint, not just authentication [A01]; (3) production debug off, non-stack-trace error pages, restrictive CORS [A05]; (4) passwords bcrypt/scrypt/argon2 with per-user salt [A02/A07]; (5) secure cookie flags [A07].\\n\\nSCOPE CAVEATS: Only the local filesystem checkout was audited; it was not verified to match PR #1\'s head commit - recommend git fetch and diff against pull/1/head. Secret scanning is pattern-based and may miss non-standard encodings, split values, or runtime-injected credentials. The CVE check detects known-vulnerable versions only, not abandoned packages, typosquatting, or newly disclosed CVEs."\n}\n```'}
